<h2 class="sec">The short answer</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>Every console version targets 30fps.</b> Rockstar confirmed that on November 10 (Game Informer), and Digital Foundry says there is no 40fps or 60fps mode on any platform.</li>
  <li><b>The PS5 Pro is the best version.</b> It renders at the same 1440p as the base PS5, but PSSR upscales it to 4K and it adds ray-traced shadows. Digital Foundry calls it the best option available, with a steadier 30.</li>
  <li><b>There's no performance mode to switch on, and none is coming.</b> Rockstar told Kotaku the game won't get one, even on the Pro (reported by Polygon).</li>
  <li><b>Base PS5 is fine, but looser.</b> Digital Foundry saw small dips in regular play and bigger ones when vehicles blow up.</li>
</ul>
<p>No performance mode, even on a Pro. Rockstar's reason is the processor, not the price tag..lol.</p>

<h2 class="sec">PS5 vs PS5 Pro vs Xbox, side by side</h2>
<p>All numbers below are from Digital Foundry's testing, which they say covered more than 100 hours across the four consoles.</p>
